Here are concise, functional Python implementations that return True if every 3-letter window has distinct characters (no repeats within any 3-letter window), and False otherwise. The length must be at least 3; otherwise, return False.

Option 1: explicit loop
- Pros: clear and efficient
- Time complexity: O(n)

def all_3_windows_distinct(s: str) -> bool:
    if len(s) < 3:
        return False
    for i in range(len(s) - 2):
        a, b, c = s[i], s[i+1], s[i+2]
        if a == b or b == c or a == c:
            return False
    return True

Option 2: using sliding window with a set
- Pros: concise
- Time complexity: O(n)

def all_3_windows_distinct(s: str) -> bool:
    if len(s) < 3:
        return False
    for i in range(len(s) - 2):
        if len({s[i], s[i+1], s[i+2]}) != 3:
            return False
    return True

